     "text": "{\"cost\": 10, \"rationale\": \"Every technique in this chain is required. Exfiltration needs admin on db, fileserver or backup. Each of those needs a foothold there plus stolen_dbadmin, so auth, escalate and exfiltrate cost 3 steps. stolen_dbadmin needs admin_dc or admin_adfs, which takes 4 more steps: kerberoast for stolen_admin, auth_dc, escalate_dc and dump_dbadmin_dc. Kerberoast needs an appserver or apiserver foothold, which takes 1 step (auth_appserver). That auth needs reach_internal (pivot_internal, 1 step) and stolen_user. phish_workstation supplies both a foothold and stolen_user in a single step. The minimal path is: phish_workstation, pivot_internal, auth_appserver, kerberoast_dc, auth_dc, escalate_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc, auth_db, escalate_db, exfiltrate_db. That is 10 techniques.\"}"
